- Reference "Owner" ↔ .NET "Owner" — ceiling Critical.
- Reference "Family"/"AuthorizedUser" ↔ .NET "AuthorizedUser" — the .NET role closest to Family is AuthorizedUser. Reference Family ceiling = Modify. Hmm, but the normative matrix says HIGH (Modify/Destructive) allows Owner/AuthorizedUser. If AuthorizedUser ceiling = Modify (per reference Family), then Destructive would be denied for AuthorizedUser — that changes current production behavior (currently AuthorizedUser with confirmation gets Destructive allowed).

